<h2 id="hr 4577">H.R. 4577</h2>

<p>H.R. 4577 is a consolidated appropriations bill for FY 2001. On December 15, 2000, the
	conference committee incorporated by reference "placeholder bills", which added
	provisions from previous tax related bills. All previous versions of H.R. 4577 are strictly
	appropriations related. This legislative history includes the original bills, placeholder
	bills and related bills to Appendix E, the "Commodity Futures Modernization Act of
	2000", Appendix G, the "Community Renewal Tax Relief Act of 2000", Appendix H, the
	"New Markets Venture Capital Program Act of 2000,"" and Appendix I, the "Small
	Business Reauthorization Act of 2000.""
		<br>
		<br>
	Appendix E: Title I covers commodity futures modernization and Title II covers the
	coordinated regulations of security futures. Title III and IV cover swap agreements and
	regulatory responsibility for bank products and were added directly to the placeholder
	bill.
		<br>
		<br>
	Appendix G: Title I substantially covers the subject of community renewal and Title III
	covers confidentiality, missing children and technical corrections.
		<br>
		<br>
	Appendix H substantially covers the New Market Venture Capital Program
		<br>
		<br>
	Appendix I: Title I covers the Small Business Innovation Research program, Title II
	covers the business loan programs, Title III covers the certified development company
	program, Title IV provides corrections to the Small Business Investment Act of 1958,
	Title V reauthorizes small business programs, and Title VI covers the HUBZone program.</p>
